<ContentLayout title="Aurora Verification" description="Build and verification evidence for the Aurora public website." eyebrow="DEVELOPMENT / VERIFICATION" heading="Evidence, not assumptions." lead="Verification reports identify what was run, against which revision, and what the result does and does not prove.">
<section class="section shell article-content"><h2>Website CI</h2><p class="content-copy">A successful GitHub Actions run for the reference-led website revision validated dependency installation, status registry validation, Astro/TypeScript checking, static build and artifact upload.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Pokejoueur/aurora-website/actions">Inspect GitHub Actions ↗</a></p><h2>What this does not prove</h2><ul class="content-list"><li>Browser-level visual correctness at every viewport.</li><li>WCAG 2.2 AA conformance or assistive-technology compatibility.</li><li>Production hosting, uptime or custom-domain configuration.</li><li>Any Aurora OS or Lumen product capability, boot result or security property.</li></ul><h2>Product verification</h2><p class="content-copy">OS and browser test reports will be published only when the relevant repositories provide reproducible evidence and a clear test scope.</p></section>
</ContentLayout>
